      "message": "Oh currently the check `usage \u003d\u003d kIndirectBufferForFrontendValidation` cannot be removed because `TrackUsageAndGetResourceBarrier()` cannot handle shader stages \u003d\u003d 0 very well. For example, with patch set 11 many tests fail because of below error:\n\nError: VUID-vkCmdPipelineBarrier-dstStageMask-03937: Validation Error: [ VUID-vkCmdPipelineBarrier-dstStageMask-03937 ] Object 0: handle \u003d 0x286c0010c200, type \u003d VK_OBJECT_TYPE_COMMAND_BUFFER; | MessageID \u003d 0x612829c1 | vkCmdPipelineBarrier(): dstStageMask must not be 0 unless synchronization2 is enabled. The Vulkan spec states: If the synchronization2 feature is not enabled, dstStageMask must not be 0 (https://www.khronos.org/registry/vulkan/specs/1.3-extensions/html/vkspec.html#VUID-vkCmdPipelineBarrier-dstStageMask-03937)",
